; WO-0033 item X-2 — the XGMII seam between the DUT-independent link-partner
; model and a live Hardcaml simulation.
;
; A separate library, and not a module of dv_xgmii, for exactly the reasons
; test/axi64_probe/dune gives for its own separation:
;
;  * dv_xgmii and dv_monitors then need no Hardcaml at all, so the link
;    partner's own tests exercise the MODEL rather than an elaboration;
;  * this is the first code in DV to name the Xgmii record's [d] and [c]
;    fields on a driven or sampled port, so if that transcription is wrong the
;    failure is confined to this directory.
;
; ifc_check is the lift of SPEC-M01 §4.1 under docs/specs/ — the signed public
; interface, byte-identical to the specification and countersigned at 22145b5.
; libs/** is not depended on and was not opened (PROTOCOL §10).
;
; hardcaml_axi is deliberately NOT a dependency: the XGMII boundary carries no
; AXI stream, and a library that linked it would be claiming a coupling the
; specification does not have.
;
; No .mli: the module is four functions whose contract is the docstring block
; at the head of xgmii_probe.ml, and an interface file here would be a second
; copy of the REQ-012 packing convention — which is precisely the drift
; Strobes' comment warns about.

(library
 (name dv_xgmii_probe)
 (inline_tests)
 (libraries hardcaml ifc_check dv_xgmii)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_expect)))
